Z||000001||batboy||09-29-1999||11:33 PM||||Thanks dude. Think I should go with a big block 454 for my next Fiero project? Actually, I'm a little embarressed about all the nice comments about my Batmobile and website. Neither one is really all that great. My V8 Fiero is kind of a plain jane, except for the 350 lurking under the rear deck lid. The website is my first and only attempt at making webpages. I kept it very simple mainly because I didn't know what I was doing. In less than two months I've had nearly 700 visits to my site. Wow! I never expected that! If you really want to get bored to tears, you can always check out my personal page:<P> <A HREF="http://sites.netscape.net/batboybain/mainpage" TARGET=_blank>http://sites.netscape.net/batboybain/mainpage</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||BlackGT||09-30-1999||11:05 AM||||Hey Batboy,<BR>Nice car....I`ve never been into the SE `s but I won`t mess with any when I see them on the road! You never know what`s lurking behind the driver. How hard was the brake swap? I have access to a well organized pull it yourself salvage yard and would like to do this when I get my car back. What do I get...keep in mind I`m mechanically challenged but don`t have a problem getting my hands dirty I just would like to know I`m pulling the necessary pieces from an 88 GrandAm.||||reg||6
Z||000003||DJRice||10-01-1999||09:29 AM||||Batboy, the batmobile looks just like my 84, except you have over twice the displacement.<BR>(and a nicer stereo)<BR>Sleepers are good, but when you get the Z28 motor in it, you will be a force to be reconed with.||||reg||1
Z||000004||batboy||10-02-1999||12:34 AM||||BlackGT, from two donor 88 Grand Am's, you need a total of 4 front rotors and 4 front calipers. But new rotors and calipers are very reasonable priced. You also need 2 pairs of brake pads, semi-metallic pads are good. <BR>This is assuming you are doing both front and rear brakes on your Fiero. A word of warning, if you do the rear, you lose the use of the emergency brake. You can do the swap on the front and then use a adjustable proportioning valve.<P>The trickiest part of the front swap is that you have to take a pair of old front Fiero rotors and have them turned down on a lathe in order to make hubs out of them. Check out this website:<P> <A HREF="http://members.tripod.com/Randy_Agee/brakes2.html" TARGET=_blank>http://members.tripod.com/Randy_Agee/brakes2.html</A> ||||reg||1
